      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 7 & 11 & 13 \\\\ 17 & 19 & 23\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -15 & 11 & 46 \\\\ -21 & 19 & 80\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of $a_{12}=3$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 7 & 11 & 13 \\\\ 17 & 19 & 23\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}-2C_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -9 \\\\ -15 & 11 & 13 \\\\ -21 & 19 & 23\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}+3C_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -15 & 11 & 46 \\\\ -21 & 19 & 80\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{1}:=C_{1}-2C_{2}$ and $C_{3}:=C_{3}+3C_{2}$.",
